<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gautama Buddha</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gautama Buddha was the founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>, who lived in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> around the fifth century BCE. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> note that Greek kingdoms in the east produced Gandharan art, in which Greek sculptural iconography was adapted to represent the Buddha and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bodhisattva">bodhisattvas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gautama-buddha.jpg" alt="Gautama Buddha" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: พระมหาเทวประภาส วชิรญาณเมธี (ผู้ถ่าย-ปล่อยสัญญาอนุญาตภาพให้นำไปใช้ได้เพื่อการศึกษาโดยอยู่ภา่ยใต้ cc-by-sa-3.0) ผู้สร้... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buddha_in_Sarnath_Museum_(Dhammajak_Mutra).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
